WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.540
28 Tesla Supercharger Bays were damaged in the largest attack yet on EV charging sites in Australia. This is Tesla Shorts Time, episode 619. Copper thieves destroyed a new ballerat station days after opening. The attack involves severing cables across multiple maze at the recently commissioned site. Local authorities are treating the incident as deliberate sabotage rather than random vandalism. Repairwork is underway. The scale of the damage has prompted

00:00:29.540 --> 00:00:33.980
increased security reviews at other stations. From physical attacks on the

00:00:33.980 --> 00:00:38.460
charging network, the focus shifts to the software and perception systems that will

00:00:38.460 --> 00:00:54.180
power future autonomy. Two patent applications numbered US2026-0285363A1 and US2026-0127891A1 address

00:00:54.180 --> 00:01:00.520
Autonomous perception. One reconstructs and remembers the static road. The other reshapes

00:01:00.520 --> 00:01:05.340
virtual viewpoints to track moving objects like vehicles, cyclists, and pedestrians.

00:01:06.120 --> 00:01:11.320
The patents cover a system that turns surround camera footage into a persistent overhead model

00:01:11.320 --> 00:01:17.980
of the road. This model keeps curves, lanes, crosswalks, and junctions visible, even when cameras

00:01:17.980 --> 00:01:23.180
lose sight of them due to obstructions. The approach relies on neural backbones that reduce

00:01:23.180 --> 00:01:29.460
images into visual features and a learned projection network that fuses them in a virtual bird's-eye space.

00:01:30.020 --> 00:01:37.780
A side-by-side test of X-pang's VLA 2.0 system against Tesla FSD took place on identical roads

00:01:37.780 --> 00:01:46.960
in Amsterdam. The first person outside of X-pang rode in an L03 prototype using XNGP with VLA 2.0

00:01:46.960 --> 00:01:50.820
followed by a Tesla Model 3 using FSD on the same routes.

00:01:51.640 --> 00:01:55.960
The comparison covers handling differences and decision making at the same intersections

00:01:55.960 --> 00:01:56.960
and route abouts.

00:01:57.560 --> 00:02:02.540
This installment marks the first part of a planned multi-part series examining both systems

00:02:02.540 --> 00:02:04.120
in real urban conditions.

00:02:04.880 --> 00:02:09.960
Observers noted variations in how each vehicle managed pedestrian crossings and lane merges

00:02:09.960 --> 00:02:11.180
during the shared drive.

00:02:11.860 --> 00:02:16.940
The test focused strictly on observable behavior rather than declared capability claims from

00:02:16.940 --> 00:02:22.540
either company. The effort is positioned as an early look at how newer vision language action

00:02:22.540 --> 00:02:28.820
models perform against established camera-only stacks. Online discussions continue to feature claims

00:02:28.820 --> 00:02:34.400
that other vehicles already match Tesla's autonomous driving performance. The post states that

00:02:34.400 --> 00:02:38.860
people asserting their cars can do the same as Tesla's features are not telling the truth.

00:02:39.520 --> 00:02:45.080
No specific competing models are named in the statement. The response targets repeated assertions

00:02:45.080 --> 00:02:49.860
appearing across social platforms about equivalent autonomy in non-Tesla vehicles.

00:02:50.500 --> 00:02:55.540
It does not provide technical breakdowns or counter-demonstrations, only a direct rebuttal

00:02:55.540 --> 00:02:56.860
of the equivalent's narrative.

00:02:57.560 --> 00:03:02.780
The comment arrives amid ongoing debates about regulatory approvals and real-world deployment

00:03:02.780 --> 00:03:04.840
timelines for supervised autonomy.

00:03:05.380 --> 00:03:10.980
A separate test examined whether the Grog bot inside a Tesla could handle an actual shopping

00:03:10.980 --> 00:03:13.360
task while the car ran on FSD.

00:03:13.360 --> 00:03:18.160
The plan called for ordering an Apple TV from Best Buy through the in-car

00:03:18.160 --> 00:03:22.680
GROC interface during the morning drive. Earlier attempts with the same bot

00:03:22.680 --> 00:03:27.400
encountered unexpected limitations that prevented successful completion. The

00:03:27.400 --> 00:03:31.540
trial is meant to check how well the assistant manages real-world commerce steps

00:03:31.540 --> 00:03:36.520
while the vehicle handles navigation and control. Observers are watching to see

00:03:36.520 --> 00:03:40.620
whether the bot can maintain context across multiple steps without driver

00:03:40.620 --> 00:03:46.220
intervention. The effort follows prior experiments that highlighted gaps between conversational

00:03:46.220 --> 00:03:51.940
ability and task execution under motion. Results from this morning's run are expected

00:03:51.940 --> 00:03:57.840
to clarify remaining constraints on voice-driven purchasing inside the car. A long-term test

00:03:57.840 --> 00:04:04.900
of the Tesla Model Y long-range began in Australia with a direct comparison to the Kia EV-9. Part

00:04:04.900 --> 00:04:10.380
1 records initial impressions after delivery and the first drives on local roads. The

00:04:10.380 --> 00:04:15.340
The evaluation centers on daily usability, how range holds up under varied conditions,

00:04:15.840 --> 00:04:17.920
and interior space versus the Kia.

00:04:18.720 --> 00:04:23.300
Early notes highlight differences in ride comfort and cargo flexibility during typical

00:04:23.300 --> 00:04:24.240
family routines.

00:04:25.080 --> 00:04:29.960
The review will continue tracking consistency of efficiency and charging behavior over the

00:04:29.960 --> 00:04:30.660
coming months.

00:04:31.380 --> 00:04:36.020
Testors are paying particular attention to how the Model Y integrates into mixed highway

00:04:36.020 --> 00:04:37.100
and suburban use.

00:04:37.100 --> 00:04:43.120
The series positions the vehicle against a popular three-row electric SUV to gauge practical

00:04:43.120 --> 00:04:49.180
ownership trade-offs. Hand assembly remains the current bottleneck even as output rises nearly

00:04:49.180 --> 00:04:55.620
tenfold. Each unit still requires manual intervention for cooling systems, battery integration,

00:04:55.920 --> 00:05:01.820
and initial AI calibration. Battery cells and actuators must reach consistent high volume

00:05:01.820 --> 00:05:07.300
availability before weekly production can approach the thousands, let alone the 20,000

00:05:07.300 --> 00:05:07.920
unit goal.

00:05:08.380 --> 00:05:13.740
Until those components move from prototype sourcing to dedicated lines, the robot's

00:05:13.740 --> 00:05:17.380
theoretical advantage in 24-hour operations stays theoretical.

00:05:18.120 --> 00:05:22.980
The practical path forward therefore runs through vertical integration on the hardware side,

00:05:23.380 --> 00:05:24.780
rather than software alone.

00:05:25.600 --> 00:05:31.720
Tesla's experience with 4680 cells and structural packs shows how controlling the full stack

00:05:31.720 --> 00:05:37.480
can compress costs, but that same discipline has yet to be applied at scale to the robot's full

00:05:37.480 --> 00:05:43.900
bill of materials. Without it, external sales remain distant even if internal deployment begins next

00:05:43.900 --> 00:05:49.700
year. Solid state batteries are entering their first practical test bed inside humanoid robots,

00:05:50.240 --> 00:05:56.260
rather than passenger cars. The choice reflects different demands on energy density and thermal stability

00:05:56.260 --> 00:05:59.260
that robots place on cells compared with vehicles.

00:06:00.020 --> 00:06:02.920
Early performance data gathered from robot duty cycles

00:06:02.920 --> 00:06:05.740
could later shape electric vehicle battery programs.

00:06:06.360 --> 00:06:09.120
Prototype packs are already undergoing evaluation

00:06:09.120 --> 00:06:12.820
for cycle life and safety under continuous operation profiles.

00:06:13.420 --> 00:06:15.680
Developers note that robot applications

00:06:15.680 --> 00:06:17.980
allow tighter control over duty cycles

00:06:17.980 --> 00:06:20.080
than mixed consumer driving patterns.

00:06:20.780 --> 00:06:23.560
The timeline for any passenger car version remains

00:06:23.560 --> 00:06:26.060
further out, while robot data accumulates.

00:06:26.900 --> 00:06:30.840
Hardware scaling challenges also appear in Tesla's newer energy offerings.

00:06:31.640 --> 00:06:34.940
Tesla is selling electricity and the fine print was reviewed.

00:06:35.540 --> 00:06:41.400
The review examines contract terms for grid export and virtual power plant participation in Australia.

00:06:42.120 --> 00:06:47.720
Customers can now sell stored energy back to the grid through Tesla's platform under specific conditions.

00:06:48.400 --> 00:06:52.320
Energy growth in one market contrasts with slower progress in another.

00:06:52.320 --> 00:06:56.740
Tesla is expanding its retail network and cutting prices in India.

00:06:57.300 --> 00:07:01.460
New showrooms are opening in Chennai and Noida to support the price reductions.

00:07:02.160 --> 00:07:08.680
Sales remain tiny despite rapid growth in the country's EV market, with only 906 registrations.

00:07:09.360 --> 00:07:14.620
The low registration count persists even as India's overall EV adoption accelerates.

00:07:15.180 --> 00:07:19.820
While established markets see infrastructure and product updates, Tesla is still laying

00:07:19.820 --> 00:07:21.260
groundwork in newer ones.

00:07:21.260 --> 00:07:25.380
Tesla may postpone the roadster unveiling due to inclement weather.

00:07:25.820 --> 00:07:31.160
The demonstration is slated for outdoors on Thursday, October 1st, to accommodate extreme

00:07:31.160 --> 00:07:36.800
features like a sub-1 second zero to 60 miles per hour launch, powered by rocket thrusters.

00:07:37.480 --> 00:07:41.640
Outdoor conditions are required because the vehicle's performance demonstrations involve

00:07:41.640 --> 00:07:45.100
high-speed maneuvers that cannot be safely shown indoors.

00:07:45.860 --> 00:07:50.540
Weather concerns center on rain that could affect the asphalt surface and visibility during

00:07:50.540 --> 00:07:55.340
the launch sequence. The article frames the vehicle's pricing and timing against broader

00:07:55.340 --> 00:08:00.700
economic and political conditions in the United States. The piece questions the optics of

00:08:00.700 --> 00:08:06.160
introducing a high-cost sports car during an election cycle. An electric car built in Greece

00:08:06.160 --> 00:08:11.060
decades before Tesla reached production used locally available technology of its era.

00:08:11.720 --> 00:08:16.540
The project predates modern EV development by many years and was assembled without

00:08:16.540 --> 00:08:22.460
access to today's battery supply chains. Contemporary reports placed the vehicle within early

00:08:22.460 --> 00:08:28.440
European experiments in electric mobility. Details on range, top speed, and production numbers

00:08:28.440 --> 00:08:34.760
remain limited in surviving records. The story highlights that electric propulsion ideas circulated

00:08:34.760 --> 00:08:40.880
long before current commercial programs. Historians note the Greek effort as one of several regional

00:08:40.880 --> 00:08:43.960
attempts that did not scale into sustained manufacturing.

00:08:44.620 --> 00:08:50.080
A 12-day rental in Oregon and Washington convinced the renters to buy a Model Y and use

00:08:50.080 --> 00:08:50.780
FSD.

00:08:51.540 --> 00:08:55.280
The experience included highway and city driving across two states.

00:08:55.880 --> 00:09:00.720
The couple cited consistent performance and convenience as reasons for the purchase decision.

